  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0017","idiomatic","Soon afterward he asked to step down and was appointed Supernumerary.","Soon afterward he asked to step down and was appointed Specially Advanced.","s0017 has 拜特進; 特進 is the Tang honorary title Specially Advanced. Rendering it as Supernumerary invents a different office and conflicts with the chapter’s own use of that English for other titles.","high","applied"],
    ["s0017","literal","Shortly thereafter he requested to yield his position and was appointed Supernumerary.","Shortly thereafter he requested to yield his position and was appointed Specially Advanced.","The literal’s appointment phrase matches 拜特進; Specially Advanced is the correct rendering of 特進, whereas Supernumerary is a different office title.","high","applied"],
    ["s0018","idiomatic","All extant editions now read \"Supernumerary.\"","All extant editions now read \"Specially Advanced.\"","s0018 says 今諸本並云特進, quoting the office-name 特進; the English quote must read Specially Advanced, not Supernumerary.","high","applied"],
    ["s0018","literal","Now all editions uniformly read \"Supernumerary.\"","Now all editions uniformly read \"Specially Advanced.\"","The literal likewise quotes 特進 from 並云特進; replacing Supernumerary with Specially Advanced restores the correct office name in the quotation.","high","applied"],
    ["s0037","idiomatic","〈At that time Chen Shou and Chen Ye were appointed to supervise; Right Remonstrator and Direct Historian of the History Office Zhang Guan and others carried out the collation.","〈At that time Ministers Shou and Ye were appointed to supervise; Right Remonstrator and Direct Historian of the History Office Zhang Guan and others carried out the collation.","臣綬、臣燁 uses 臣 as the memorial self-reference “minister/your servant,” not the surname Chen; Ministers Shou and Ye matches the Chinese and the existing literal.","high","applied"]
